# Spacio Server Rules (NestJS 12 & WebSockets)

## 1. Directory Structure
Enforce strict separation within `src/`:
- `core/`: Global configurations, database providers, and Redis Pub/Sub adapters.
- `shared/`: Shared DTOs, domain interfaces, custom decorators, and global filters/guards.
- `gateway/`: Socket.io gateway handlers for multi-user scene state, cursor/presence sync, and room locking.
- `modules/`: Feature modules (e.g., `spatial-parser`, `room-persistence`, `ai-generator`).

## 2. NestJS 12 Standards
- **Strongly Typed Payloads:** Validate all incoming WebSocket payloads and REST requests using `class-validator` and `class-transformer` decorated DTOs.
- **Modular Gateways:** Keep Socket.io event listener methods lean by delegating transformation, spatial validation, and state persistence to injected domain services.
- **Stateless Cloud Design:** Keep server memory lean and stateless to support deployment on Render free-tier infrastructure using Redis for room state distribution.